{
  "summary": "Florida Statute 627.062 sets rate standards for covered insurance classes, prohibiting rates that are excessive, inadequate, or unfairly discriminatory. It establishes rate filing procedures, review factors for the insurance office, special provisions for fire, property/casualty, residential property, medical malpractice, and high-value residential coverage, and related refund, certification, hearing, and rate-increase limitations.",
